{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:96184550f43ae661","name":"Terentatek","source":{"id":"source:reference-96184550f43ae661","title":"Terentatek","revision":20551,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:04:13Z","sha256":"eecad1edb27f636b2960f29cfaf60bab15f893ba1133032d0e0c308a147a81ab","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20551","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Terentatek&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-96184550f43ae661","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The dreaded Terentatek greatly resembles the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rancor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rancor","referenceId":"reference:fb68a8b2803a85f7"},", with large spines jutting from its back and an additional set of mandibles sprouting from its mouth. It has been theorized that Terentateks were once ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rancors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rancors"}," that were subjugated to experimentation by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},". They are typically found in locations tainted by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", such as the tombs on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"},". Because of their remarkable immunity to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", Terentateks are also known as \"Jedi Killers.\"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," is weaker in the galaxy, Terentateks go into hibernation, which can sometimes last for hundreds or even thousands of years. When ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," increases in power, Terentateks emerge from their slumber to threaten their surroundings. Jedi are known to hunt in small teams to eliminate the Terentatek menace.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Terentatek Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Terentateks are rarely encountered alone. They usually patrol their territory in mated pairs, making encounters with them all that more dangerous. Terentateks are not subtle and simply charge opponents. Despite their Force immunity, Terentateks do not favor Jedi or other Force-users over other prey and attack the closest or more aggressive targets first, although the bright light and noise from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," quickly grabs their attention.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Terentatek Statistics (CL 14)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge Subterranean ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 34 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze